# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Jan Weinreich et al. (2020). Properties of $α$-Brass Nanoparticles I: Neural Network Potential Energy Surface.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2001.10906  arXiv:2001.10906v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2001.10906v2 (sha256 7bcf7d95a4d623e2...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 559 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/weinreich2020.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: RuNNer HDNNPs for Cu-Zn (alpha-brass) trained on
# 53,841 PBE structures (bulk, slabs, cut-out clusters of 179-344 atoms,
# molten structures) selected by committee disagreement; training and
# test RMSEs for five atomic-network architectures (Table 2, 20-20
# selected). Bulk, surface, cluster melting and cohesive-energy results
# are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
